{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyFxcr5Jk53zjQeSWLB8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan to Wire `check:pricing-sync` into Pre-Commit Hook\n\n1. **Check if pre-commit hook already exists**\n   - Look for `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (or `husky` config if the repo uses it)\n   - Determine the current hook mechanism (shell script, husky, lefthook, etc.)\n\n2. **Verify the check works locally**\n   - Run `npm run check:pricing-sync` once to confirm it exists and passes/fails deterministically\n\n3. **Add the check to the hook**\n   - If using husky: add entry to `.husky/pre-commit`\n   - If using shell script: append the command to `.git/hooks/pre-commit`\n   - If no hook exists: create one (or initialize husky if that's the team pattern)\n   - Ensure the hook calls `npm run check:pricing-sync` and exits non-zero on failure\n\n4. **Make the hook executable**\n   - Run `chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit` (or verify husky handles this)\n\n5. **Test the hook blocks commits**\n   - Intentionally break one of the two files\n   - Attempt `git commit` and verify it rejects the commit\n   - Restore the file to confirm hook allows commit when check passes\n\n6. **Document and commit**\n   - Commit the hook changes (or hook config file) with a clear message\n   - Update `CONTRIBUTING.md` or similar if the repo has developer onboarding docs"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":348,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
